[1.750282, "o", "Initialized mnema project at ~/your-repository/.mnema\r\n  identity: mnid:b41785cb3473b7cdca53b949bfeb6be9e9c26e0eed1fd1e8fbcd6a8a2c21d1e7\r\n"]
[1.750467, "o", "  backup key: created and enrolled, private half at ~/.mnema/identity/backup/1c361168ad893962ff228ce51b529a5a3ca37906f5b08ea9405bf2e158a0df74.key\r\n  Move that file off this machine: a backup left on this disk is lost with it.\r\n"]
[1.750956, "o", "  Created AGENTS.md, with the mnema instructions.\r\n"]
[1.750998, "o", "  Created .claude/rules/mnema-instructions.md, with the mnema instructions.\r\n  Created .github/instructions/mnema-instructions.instructions.md, with the mnema instructions.\r\n"]
[1.751015, "o", "  Created .cursor/rules/mnema-instructions.mdc, with the mnema instructions.\r\n"]
[1.751131, "o", "  Each holds the mnema instructions an agent host reads at the start of a session: when to\r\n"]
[1.75123, "o", "  call the mnema tools, and what never goes in the record. `mnema instructions --remove`\r\n  takes them out.\r\n"]
[1.751571, "o", "\r\n  mnema writes no other file of yours. In Claude Code the mnema plugin hands this record to\r\n  each session on its own. Without it, `mnema brief > MNEMA.md` puts what governs this\r\n  project in a file of its own (the `>` replaces the whole of the file it names), and\r\n  one line in a `CLAUDE.md` brings that file in (an `AGENTS.md` is read there only\r\n  where no `CLAUDE.md` exists):\r\n    @MNEMA.md\r\n\r\n  Commit `.mnema/` with the repository: the record travels with it, and every clone reads it.\r\n  Off until switched on: edit-first-write-gate, user-corrections.\r\n  Turn one on with `mnema switch on <name>`; `mnema switch` lists every channel.\r\n  Next: `mnema decision record <title> <rationale>`; `mnema status` shows where things stand.\r\n"]
[3.37275, "o", "\u001b[2m# write down a call, with the reasoning and what was turned down\u001b[0m\r\n"]
